    "created_at": "2017-11-23T07:58:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-23T07:58:05Z",
    "body": "Maybe you're tripping over semantics here. with \"file name\" I meant the extension visible in a URL -- and it was an example indicating that apart from sniffing, a client can determine/guess the content type in other ways when not being specified with a header.\r\n\r\nI'm not going to spend much more time on this issue, though, I have better things to do -- My point remains that the spec could be clarified and made completely unambiguous with a one-line change. Ultimately, it's the editor's choice to do or not do this.",
